From a85a7cbaee08ddae5f4f339a5912c9ce1fb55d72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:00:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] qwen4exp seqpar: default on (LLAMA_SEQPAR=0 /
 LLAMA_SEQPAR_GATHER_BF16=0 off), diagnostics

- LLAMA_SEQPAR and the bf16 hc_mixed gather wire are on by default; LLAMA_SEQPAR=0 restores the
  unsplit graph exactly, LLAMA_SEQPAR_GATHER_BF16=0 keeps the F32 wire.
- Not engaged: one INFO line per context and reason (LLAMA_SEQPAR=0, not -sm tensor, a layer not on
  exactly 2 devices, a drafter reading per-layer inputs, ubatch below LLAMA_SEQPAR_MIN / odd with
  LLAMA_SEQPAR_ODD=0). Keyed per context, not per process: common's --fit builds trial contexts
  with INFO demoted, which spent process-wide once-flags (the 0004 engage line never printed).
  The MIN check now precedes the per-layer walk, so decode and verify graphs stop early.
- Executed-form census (meta backend): cumulative counts of reduce-scatter by the comm backend /
  all-reduce + slice / fallback all-reduce + slice and token all_gather by the comm backend /
  generic copies, logged when a form first runs (one compute per scheduler split, so a per-compute
  mix would repeat every ubatch). The graph-time line now says "fold an all-reduce" (eligible).
- CUDA: the copy-engine reduce-scatter / all_gather log each decline reason once. The CE scratch
  reserve takes its caller: a seqpar collective that cannot get the scratch warns with its own
  message and flag (all-reduce + slice / generic copies) instead of the all-reduce's, which it no
  longer consumes. Scratch growth is logged (raw device memory outside the ggml allocators).
- CUDA: the reduce-scatter selects the default chain's large arm before deciding, as the
  all-reduce does; before, a reduce-scatter ahead of the first large all-reduce took the copy
  engine with host experts while the rest followed the RCCL ring.
